# Sellerboard -> Power BI. The server clock is America/New_York.
# UK  (account Uk-AMZ)              -> powerbidb.Uk_breakdown_data
# US  (account premiumcarproduct)   -> powerbidb.Sellerboard_breakdown_data_2024 (--us-premium)
# Both jobs use one Sellerboard login and switch its account, so they must never run at the same time.
# `timeout -k 1m 20m` stops a hung run, so it can never overlap the next one. A failed run only writes
# its log and exits; it never stops the other job.
# Install with `crontab -e`, replacing older Sellerboard lines. Use absolute paths (`which uv`).
MAILTO=""

# Option A: every 30 minutes, including today's numbers (set SELLERBOARD_INCLUDE_TODAY=true in .env).
# UK at :00 and :30, US at :15 and :45 -- 15 minutes apart, so they never overlap.
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< UK-Product-Breakdown-Data Start >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
0,30 * * * * cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 12m /root/.local/bin/uv run python run.py --uk-amazon --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
15,45 * * * * cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 12m /root/.local/bin/uv run python run.py --us-premium --quiet >> logs/cron-output-us.log 2>&1
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< UK-Product-Breakdown-Data End >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>

# Option B: once a day at 13:00 / 13:30 IST, full days only. The time check keeps it right when
# New York changes between summer (EDT) and winter (EST) time. Keep the backslashes before %.
# 30 2,3 * * * [ "$(TZ=Asia/Kolkata date +\%H\%M)" = "1300" ] && cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 20m /root/.local/bin/uv run python run.py --uk-amazon --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
# 0 3,4 * * * [ "$(TZ=Asia/Kolkata date +\%H\%M)" = "1330" ] && cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 20m /root/.local/bin/uv run python run.py --us-premium --quiet >> logs/cron-output-us.log 2>&1
